⭐ FULL 3‑TIER DEPLOYMENT IN AWS (GUI) — USING SSM ONLY
(No SSH, no port 22, no public EC2 instances)

1️⃣ Create the VPC
Go to VPC → Create VPC

Name: three-tier-ssm-vpc

IPv4 CIDR: 10.0.0.0/16

Enable DNS hostnames: Yes

2️⃣ Create Subnets
You need 6 subnets (2 per tier, across 2 AZs)

Public Subnets (for ALB + NAT)
10.0.1.0/24 (AZ1)

10.0.2.0/24 (AZ2)

Private App Subnets (for EC2 ASG)
10.0.10.0/24 (AZ1)

10.0.11.0/24 (AZ2)

Private DB Subnets (for RDS)
10.0.20.0/24 (AZ1)

10.0.21.0/24 (AZ2)

3️⃣ Internet Gateway
VPC → Internet Gateways → Create

Attach to your VPC

4️⃣ NAT Gateway
VPC → NAT Gateways → Create

Subnet: Public Subnet 1

Elastic IP: Allocate new

This allows private EC2 instances to reach SSM.

5️⃣ Route Tables
Public Route Table
Add route: 0.0.0.0/0 → Internet Gateway

Associate both public subnets

Private Route Table
Add route: 0.0.0.0/0 → NAT Gateway

Associate app + db subnets

6️⃣ Security Groups
No port 22 anywhere.

ALB SG
Inbound: 80/443 from 0.0.0.0/0

App SG
Inbound: 8080 from ALB SG

DB SG
Inbound: 5432 (Postgres) or 3306 (MySQL) from App SG

7️⃣ IAM Role for EC2 (SSM Access)
Go to IAM → Roles → Create Role

Trusted entity: EC2

Attach policy:

AmazonSSMManagedInstanceCore

Name: three-tier-ssm-ec2-role

This is what allows SSM access instead of SSH.

8️⃣ Create Launch Template (App Tier)
Go to EC2 → Launch Templates → Create

AMI: Amazon Linux 2

Instance type: t3.micro

IAM role: three-tier-ssm-ec2-role

Security group: App SG

User data (optional simple app):

Code
#!/bin/bash
yum update -y
yum install -y httpd
systemctl enable httpd
systemctl start httpd
echo "OK" > /var/www/html/health
echo "Hello from App Tier" > /var/www/html/index.html
9️⃣ Create Auto Scaling Group
Go to EC2 → Auto Scaling → Create ASG

Launch template: select the one you created

VPC: your VPC

Subnets: private app subnets

Desired: 2

Min: 2

Max: 6

Attach to target group (created in next step).

🔟 Create ALB (Web Tier)
Go to EC2 → Load Balancers → Create ALB

Type: Application Load Balancer

Scheme: Internet-facing

Subnets: both public subnets

Security group: ALB SG

Create Target Group
Type: Instance

Port: 8080

Health check: /health

Listener
HTTP 80 → Forward to target group

1️⃣1️⃣ Create RDS (DB Tier)
Go to RDS → Create Database

Engine: Postgres or MySQL

Template: Free tier or Production

Multi-AZ: optional

Credentials: choose username/password

Subnet group: select private DB subnets

Public access: NO

Security group: DB SG

1️⃣2️⃣ Verify SSM Access (No SSH Needed)
Go to Systems Manager → Fleet Manager → Nodes

You should see your EC2 instances appear.

Click Node → Connect → Start Session

You now have full shell access without port 22.

1️⃣3️⃣ Test the Application
Open the ALB DNS name:

Code
http://<your-alb-dns>
You should see:

Code
Hello from App Tier
